module test.claim.spark.spark_serving_hermetic_acquisition_fixture

// ONE HERMETIC ACQUISITION AUTHORITY FOR EVERY WITNESS THAT NEEDS A PROVENANCE.
//
// Four witness files each declared their own `witness_provenance`, and all four answered with the
// HERMETIC arm -- so every planning claim in the corpus was made against a provenance that
// production planning is required to refuse. That is two defects wearing one helper: the same fact
// authored four times (one concept, four authorities), and a fixture whose arm is not the arm the
// route under test accepts, so the claims could only ever exercise the refusal path or a route that
// existed to bypass it.
//
// This module is the single authority. It builds an ACQUIRED provenance the only way one can be
// built -- through the sealed transaction mint, over a complete capture roster -- with every input
// hermetic and every derivation real. Nothing here asserts a credential or an attempt: the
// credential comes out of the production classifier having established the key equality, and the
// fleet attempt is parsed rather than cast, so an unparseable literal refuses here exactly as it
// would in acquisition.
//
// The refused and fixture arms are also offered, because a witness that wants to prove planning
// REFUSES a non-acquired observation needs to author one.

